  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "through-runtime",
      "claim": "Anthropic Messages and Azure OpenAI Chat and streams go through the llmgw-core Runtime with core's Anthropic and Azure OpenAI verticals, registered in the per-type table. Anthropic Chat keeps the gateway's llm-translate conversion and then invokes the vertical on Messages, re-encoding its events into the Chat chunks the gateway produced before; token counts go through core.CountTokens. Azure Chat stays labelled translated. The gateway's Anthropic Messages, streamed-completion, count and stream transports and Azure's Chat and stream transports are removed; Zen's store is generalized as connectionStore with Zen unchanged.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/anthropic_vertical.go, azure_vertical.go, anthropic.go, azureopenai.go; go/internal/api/testdata unchanged"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "credentials",
      "claim": "Credentials resolve in the same order as before (caller connection, system connection, configured key), keyless Anthropic still allowed; setup-token connections load as core.TokenTypeAnthropicSetupToken and a configured key with the setup-token prefix is still sent as one; Azure accepts API keys only.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/iam/credential_record.go; go/internal/providers anthropic and azure tests"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "deviations",
      "claim": "Edge-case differences: an Azure request with no key is refused before sending (500 misconfigured instead of Azure's 401, and a Messages chain may move past it); a trailing slash in an Anthropic base URL no longer produces a double slash and an invalid URL is refused instead of panicking; an Anthropic Chat answer followed by stray bytes is accepted; a token count above int64 is invalid; credentials resolve per request; Azure refuses redirects off the resource; closing an Anthropic Chat stream now ends its upstream read.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers anthropic and azure tests"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "suite",
      "claim": "The full Go suite passes with HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY unreachable with unchanged characterization goldens and coupling budgets; gofmt, vet, govulncheck (0 reachable), check-docs and git diff --check pass.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "local gate run on the reviewed head"
      }
    }
  ],
